## 2026-06-12: GameObjectSwitchToggle implementation baseline

### Confirmed local evidence

- `GameObjectSwitchToggle` is under `Assets/Game/UI/ShopPanel/Scripts/` and currently has serialized `TriggerBtn`, `OnPart`, and `OffPart` fields.
- The current class summary requests three behaviors: switch On/Off state, show one part at a time, and provide an `IsOnCallback`.
- `CustomButton` exposes an `OnClick` event and blocks clicks when inactive, non-interactable, delayed, or click-blocked.
- `ShopPanelSwitchGroup` already uses an `_isBound` guard plus `OnDisable`/`OnDestroy` cleanup around `CustomButton.OnClick` subscriptions.
- `ShopPanelSwitchGroup` is ShopPanel-specific and controls `ShopPart`/`SkinPart` tab visuals; `GameObjectSwitchToggle` planning keeps the helper generic and does not replace ShopPanel purchase, ad, restore, save, config, analytics, or resource-loading behavior.
- `GameObjectSwitchToggle` now resolves initial state from assigned part activity only when exactly one part is active; ambiguous both-active or both-inactive states fall back to Off.
- `GameObjectSwitchToggle` now binds `TriggerBtn.OnClick` in `OnEnable`, unbinds in `OnDisable` and `OnDestroy`, and guards duplicate subscription with `_isBound`.
- `GameObjectSwitchToggle` now exposes `IsOn`, `Toggle()`, `SetIsOn(bool)`, `SetOn()`, `SetOff()`, serialized `BoolEvent IsOnCallback`, and runtime `Action<bool> OnIsOnChanged`.
- `GameObjectSwitchToggle` now also exposes `SetIsOnWithoutNotify(bool)` for group-style callers that need to synchronize visual state without recursively dispatching change callbacks.
- `GameObjectSwitchToggle` applies state through null-safe `SetActiveIfNeeded(...)` and only invokes callbacks after an effective state change.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` owns the ShopPanel skin switch `switchToggles` list and binds each toggle through `OnIsOnChanged` on enable, with cleanup on disable/destroy.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` now applies ToggleGroup-style exclusive selection: when one configured `GameObjectSwitchToggle` turns on, all other configured toggles are turned off through `SetIsOnWithoutNotify(bool)`.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart.allowSwitchOff = false` keeps at least one configured toggle on; if all toggles are off during enable-time normalization, `defaultOnIndex` is selected when valid, otherwise the first non-null toggle is selected.
- `GameObjectToggleGroup` is under `Assets/Game/UI/ShopPanel/Scripts/` and provides a generic exclusive group for serialized `GameObjectSwitchToggle` entries.
- `GameObjectToggleGroup` binds each configured toggle through `OnIsOnChanged` on enable and clears subscriptions in `OnDisable` and `OnDestroy`.
- `GameObjectToggleGroup` keeps at most one configured toggle on by applying non-selected toggle states through `SetIsOnWithoutNotify(bool)` and guarding recursive callback handling with `_isApplyingGroupState`.
- `GameObjectToggleGroup.allowSwitchOff = false` prevents the selected toggle from remaining off after a user click; `allowSwitchOff = true` allows `ClearSelection()` and all-off state.
- `GameObjectToggleGroup` exposes `SelectedToggle`, `SelectedIndex`, `SelectToggle(...)`, `SelectToggleWithoutNotify(...)`, `SelectIndex(...)`, `ClearSelection()`, `RegisterToggle(...)`, `UnregisterToggle(...)`, serialized `SelectionChangedCallback`, and runtime `Action<GameObjectSwitchToggle> OnSelectionChanged`.
- `ShopPanelSwitchGroup` now combines its Shop/Skin tab content switching with the `GameObjectToggleGroup` selection API when a group is available on the same object; the component keeps a direct `GameObjectSwitchToggle.OnIsOnChanged` fallback only for prefab variants without `GameObjectToggleGroup`.
- `ShopPanelSwitchGroup` resolves `Shop_toggle` and `Skin_toggle`, listens to `GameObjectToggleGroup.OnSelectionChanged` in the current ShopPanel prefab path, and uses `SelectToggleWithoutNotify(...)` during internal state synchronization to avoid recursive callbacks.
- `ShopPanelSwitchGroup` no longer keeps the old `ShopOn_Btn`, `ShopOff_Btn`, `SkinOn_Btn`, and `SkinOff_Btn` fallback fields; it now depends on `GameObjectSwitchToggle` for tab visual synchronization.
- Static scan found no `DB`, `Save`, `RemoteConfig`, `Instance`, `Instantiate`, `OnValidate`, `Reset`, `ExecuteAlways`, or `ExecuteInEditMode` usage in `Assets/Game/UI/ShopPanel/Scripts/GameObjectSwitchToggle.cs`.
- Static scan found no `DB`, `Save`, `RemoteConfig`, `Instance`, `Instantiate`, `OnValidate`, `Reset`, `ExecuteAlways`, or `ExecuteInEditMode` usage in `Assets/Game/UI/ShopPanel/Scripts/ShopPanel_SkinPart.cs`.
- Static scan found no `DB`, `Save`, `RemoteConfig`, `Instance`, `Instantiate`, `OnValidate`, `Reset`, `ExecuteAlways`, or `ExecuteInEditMode` usage in `Assets/Game/UI/ShopPanel/Scripts/GameObjectToggleGroup.cs`.
- Static scan found no `DB`, `Save`, `RemoteConfig`, `Instance`, `Instantiate`, `OnValidate`, `Reset`, `ExecuteAlways`, or `ExecuteInEditMode` usage in `Assets/Game/UI/ShopPanel/Scripts/ShopPanelSwitchGroup.cs`.
- `ShopPanel.prefab` contains `GameObjectSwitchToggle` on `SkinPartToggle` with `TriggerBtn`, `OnPart`, and `OffPart` references assigned; `IsOnCallback` currently has no persistent calls.
- `ShopPanel.prefab` contains `ShopPanel_SkinPart` on `SkinPart` with four configured `switchToggles` entries for the skin toggle objects.
- `ShopPanel.prefab` contains `GameObjectSwitchToggle` on `Shop_toggle` and `Skin_toggle`, with the tab `TriggerBtn`, `OnPart`, and `OffPart` references assigned for Shop/Skin tab visual roots.
- Static compile check passed via `dotnet build Assembly-CSharp.csproj --no-restore`: 0 errors / 90 existing project warnings.

### Pending validation

- Unity PlayMode still needs to verify `GameObjectSwitchToggle` initial state resolution, trigger toggling, callback dispatch, missing-reference behavior, repeated enable/disable cleanup, and actual `ShopPanel.prefab` usage.
- Unity PlayMode still needs to verify `GameObjectToggleGroup` exclusive selection, `allowSwitchOff` true/false behavior, default selection fallback, `ClearSelection()`, runtime register/unregister, selection callback dispatch, and repeated enable/disable cleanup.
- Unity PlayMode still needs to verify `ShopPanel_SkinPart` exclusive selection, `allowSwitchOff=false` reselection behavior, default selection behavior, and repeated close/reopen event cleanup.
- Unity PlayMode still needs to verify `ShopPanelSwitchGroup` Shop/Skin tab switching through the `GameObjectSwitchToggle` path, active-tab re-click behavior, and repeated close/reopen event cleanup.
- ShopPanel regression still needs PlayMode verification for shop goods, purchase, ad, restore, close, and sold-out behavior after interacting with the helper-controlled visuals.
- Android/iOS landscape smoke still needs to verify touch behavior and no visible overlap or hitch when the helper is attached to production UI.

