## 2026-06-12: UIGenerator sprite fallback search

### Confirmed local evidence

- `UIGenerator` is an editor tool under `Assets/BearGame/com.bear.ui@919f05cf0418/Editor/UIGenerator/` for generating UI prefabs from supported JSON exports.
- `UIGeneratorSettings` stores the default settings asset at `Assets/Resources/UIGeneratorSettings.asset` and exposes `defaultSpriteFolder`.
- `UIGenerator.GenerateUIPrefab(...)` supports both PSD-style `document + layers` JSON and legacy Artboard array JSON.
- Image sprite resolution first tries direct/local JSON paths and then falls back to configured default sprite folders.
- The fallback folder cache includes `defaultSpriteFolder` itself and all descendant directories named `Sprites`.
- The image fallback path now also recursively searches all child folders under each candidate fallback directory, so files under nested folders inside `Sprites` can fill generated Image sprites.
- Multi-sprite texture assets still load by matching the sprite sub-asset name before falling back to the first sprite in the asset.
- Project-side `UIGeneratorGamePostProcessor` calls `UIGeneratorUIViewScriptGenerator.GenerateFromPrefabHierarchy(...)` after prefab save; when the matching UI View type does not exist, the generator now asks whether to create the main view script and `.Generated.cs` binding script before writing files.
- Choosing Skip in that script-generation dialog only skips script creation and does not cancel the prefab save or other UIGenerator post-processing.
- This change is editor tooling only and does not modify runtime UI loaders, save/config data, platform SDK settings, shipped level scripts, or UI prefabs.

### Pending validation

- Unity Editor still needs to verify generation for a `src`-based image where the matching file exists only under `Sprites/<child>/`.
- Unity Editor still needs to verify legacy layer-name image generation where the matching file exists only under `Sprites/<child>/`.
- Unity Editor still needs to verify the missing-script dialog appears only when the matching UI View type is absent, and that Generate/Skip produce the expected script-generation behavior.
- Unity Editor still needs to verify duplicate file-name behavior in multiple nested folders if deterministic priority becomes important for production use.
- Android/iOS runtime smoke is not required for this editor-only lookup change, but generated prefabs should still be checked normally before shipping UI changes.

## 2026-06-10: Level59 double-touch scale input

