### Confirmed local evidence

- `SimpleAudioPlay` is added under `Assets/Game/Scripts/Level/LevelItem/Level_63/` as a Level63-local runtime MonoBehaviour.
- The helper exposes serialized `clipName`, `loop`, `loopInterval`, `playOnStart`, and `stopSoundOnDisable` fields for Inspector configuration.
- `playOnStart` triggers playback only from runtime `Start()`.
- `PlayAudio()` uses the existing `Game.Scripts.Common.AudioManager.PlaySound(...)` SFX path and does not modify shared `AudioManager`.
- `loop=true` with `loopInterval <= 0` uses the existing continuous SoundsGood loop path and stores the returned `Sound` for stopping.
- `loop=true` with `loopInterval > 0` repeats one-shot playback from a local coroutine.
- `SimpleAudioPlay` stores the latest returned `Sound`, including one-shot playback, so `StopAudio()` can stop the current sound.
- `stopSoundOnDisable` defaults true; when false, disable stops only the local interval coroutine and lets the current sound continue.
- `OnDestroy` always calls `StopAudio()` to stop the local coroutine and owned current sound.
- Static compile check passed again after adding `stopSoundOnDisable` via `dotnet build Assembly-CSharp.csproj --no-restore`: 0 errors / 89 existing warnings.
- Static compile check passed via `dotnet build Assembly-CSharp.csproj --no-restore`: 0 errors / 89 existing warnings.

