## 2026-06-10: Level62 Block selection actor-contact semantics

### Confirmed local evidence

- `Level62Ctrl.cs` keeps one active touch for Level62 selection; additional simultaneous touches are ignored until the first active touch ends.
- `Level62Ctrl` uses `SP_L62_xzk_img_02` as the drag selector visual name and updates the selector through `SpriteRenderer.drawMode = Sliced` plus `SpriteRenderer.size`.
- Direct tap selection selects the tapped `Level62BlockItemCtrl` and deselects other configured block items in the same controller list.
- Area selection starts from empty space and selects block items whose center point is inside the selector rectangle; it adds to the current selected set without clearing selected blocks outside the area.
- `Level62BlockItemCtrl.SetSelected(true)` shows selectBox, sets unbroken block alpha to 1, and calls `SpriteRenderFragilePlatform.SetActorContactEnabled(true)`.
- `Level62BlockItemCtrl.SetSelected(false)` hides selectBox, sets unbroken block alpha to 0.7, and calls `SpriteRenderFragilePlatform.SetActorContactEnabled(false)`.
- `SpriteRenderFragilePlatform` is local to `Assets/Game/Scripts/Level/LevelItem/Level_62/`; repository search found no other level script references to the class.
- `SpriteRenderFragilePlatform` now uses `BreakState.Intact/Breaking`; selected actor contact starts a configurable `contactBreakDelaySeconds` delay while keeping collider contact enabled, then disables collider, fades for `fadeOutDuration`, and restores visible unselected state instead of destroying the platform. Later selection changes do not cancel or reset an already breaking/fading platform.
- `Level62Ctrl` no longer depends on the platform collider for player tap selection; it resolves touched blocks through configured block visible `SpriteRenderer.bounds` so unselected blocks can keep actor contact disabled while remaining selectable by the player.
- `SpriteRenderFragilePlatform` keeps `SetAutoBreak(...)` / `GetAutoBreak()` as compatibility wrappers and uses `FormerlySerializedAs("autoBreak")` to migrate the old serialized field into `actorContactEnabled`.

### Pending validation

- Unity Editor PlayMode still needs to verify `Level_062.prefab` block list, selectBox, selectorBox, Collider2D, and fragilePlatform runtime references.
- PlayMode still needs to verify direct tap selection, four drag directions, empty-area selection, additive area selection, multi-touch ignore, and restart/fail/exit/completion cleanup.
- PlayMode still needs to verify `SP_L62_xzk_img_02` Sprite border/slice settings support sliced-size selector visuals.
- PlayMode still needs to verify selected alpha 1 and unselected alpha 0.7 coverage.
- PlayMode still needs to verify unselected blocks prevent actor contact while still being selectable by player tap.
- PlayMode still needs to verify selected actor contact remains collidable for `contactBreakDelaySeconds`, then closes collider, fades for `fadeOutDuration`, and restores visible unselected state after fade completion.
- PlayMode still needs to verify breaking/fading platforms are not reset early by later selection changes.
- PlayMode still needs to confirm restart/re-entry behavior if it occurs while a Level62 block is in the contact-delay or fading flow.
- Android / iOS landscape touch and device performance still need validation.

