## 2026-06-15: ShopPanel infinite skin scroll implementation

### Confirmed local evidence

- `InfiniteScrollView` is added under `Assets/Game/UI/ShopPanel/Scripts/` as a ShopPanel-local bounded-slot `ScrollRect` adapter.
- `InfiniteScrollView` exposes `InfiniteScrollMode.Finite` and `InfiniteScrollMode.Cyclic`; cyclic mode becomes effective only when catalog count is greater than visible slot capacity.
- `InfiniteScrollView` creates visible slots only during explicit rebuild/initialization, keeps a bounded slot list, rebinds slots through `(SkinItem, itemIndex)`, and resets to the beginning on full refresh.
- `InfiniteScrollView.OnValidate()` only clamps local serialized layout values and does not access DB, config, singleton managers, runtime resources, or instantiate objects.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` keeps the existing `GameObjectSwitchToggle` exclusive filter behavior and adds all/back/face/body catalog filtering.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` reads `ConfigManager.Instance?.Tables.TbSkin` and `TbSkinShop` during runtime catalog rebuild, passes count and bind callback into `InfiniteScrollView`, and does not write save/config/analytics state.
- `SkinItem` now binds one `Config.Skin` row, clears stale title/icon/selected/coin/ad/default/interactable state before each bind, and routes clicks through the currently bound skin row.
- `ShopPanel.prefab` wires `ShopPanel_SkinPart` to the skin scroll component, ScrollRect, and `SkinItem.prefab`; the existing four skin filter toggle references remain assigned.
- `SkinItem.prefab` assigns `BlockBg`, `icon`, `title`, `selected`, `coinPart`, `adPart`, `defaultPart`, and `btn` serialized references.
- `dotnet build BrainPunk/Assembly-CSharp.csproj --no-restore` completed with 0 errors after the implementation.

### Pending validation

- Unity PlayMode still needs to verify ShopPanel Skin open, list reset, finite/cyclic scrolling, no gaps/overlaps, slot reuse, filter mapping, current-entry click routing, and close/reopen cleanup.
- ShopPanel regression still needs PlayMode verification for shop goods, purchase, rewarded-ad, restore, sold-out, reward animation, and busy-state close behavior after using Skin scroll.
- Android/iOS landscape smoke still needs to verify touch drag/flick feel, viewport clipping, no stale entries during rapid direction changes, and no unbounded active UI growth.
- `SkinItem` icon resource display currently keeps the assigned/fallback sprite state only; actual skin icon/resource resolution remains pending a later visual resource binding decision.

## 2026-06-15: ShopPanel Skin version2.0.0 unlock/apply flow

### Confirmed local evidence

- `Config.Skin` provides `Id`, `SkinName`, `SkinPart`, `PrefabResource`, `SpineResource`, `UnlockType`, `Quality`, `UnlockHint`, `CoinPrice`, and `ProductId` fields.
- `GameData` exposes skin ownership and current selection fields: `OwnedSkin`, `CurrentBackPart`, `CurrentFacePart`, `CurrentBodyPart`, and `CurrentSkinId`. 2026-06-23 correction: earlier records named this full-body field `CurrentSkinName`, but current code exposes `CurrentSkinId`.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` now ensures `SkinUnlockType.Default` rows are present in `DB.GameData.OwnedSkin` during runtime refresh/open and saves only when the default ownership list changes.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` currently treats owned skins as directly applicable: back/face/body rows write the matching part field, other rows write `CurrentSkinId`, then save and refresh the viewer/list state. 2026-06-23 note: SkinPart v2.0 planning changes the target behavior to preview-first clicks, so this remains the current baseline.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` handles `SkinUnlockType.Ad` with `RewardAdHelper.TryToShowRewardAd(RewardPlacement.ShopReward.ToString())`; the selected skin is captured before the async ad callback so later UI selection changes do not redirect the reward.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` handles `SkinUnlockType.Coin` by checking `PlayCtrl.Instance?.Bag.GetToolCount(GameProps.Coin)`, showing `U_HurryTips_NeedCoin` on insufficient coin, and spending through `RemoveTool(GameProps.Coin, price, CostType.Other)` before granting the skin.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` handles `SkinUnlockType.Purchase` through the existing product-name path: `Products.GetProductId(skin.ProductId)`, `GameSDKService.Instance?.IAP_CLK(productId.Sku)`, and `GameManager.Instance.Purchase.Purchase(skin.ProductId, "skin", OnSkinPurchaseCallback)`.
- Skin purchase success grants only the selected skin ownership and current selection. It does not call `PurchaseManager.OnPurchaseSuccess(...)` because the skin reward is not resolved through `TbShop.Rewards` in the current implementation.
- Ad and purchase unlock success play `AudioManager.PlaySound("shopGetReward")`; purchase success also shows `U_HurryTips_Shop_succeed`.
- `SkinItem` now hides coin/ad/default unlock indicators for owned rows, keeps unavailable rows non-interactable, and applies the version2.0.0 selected-state requirement by scaling `BlockBg` to `1.1` while restoring the original scale on reuse/clear.
- `UISpineCtrl` now supports `SetCombinedSkin(IEnumerable<string>)` by finding each named Spine skin, combining valid entries with `Spine.Skin.AddSkin(...)`, and applying setup-pose reset after success.
- `GameObjectToggleGroup` owns the skin filter exclusive-selection behavior. `ShopPanel_SkinPart` now listens to the group's selected index and only maps the result to all/back/face/body filtering; it no longer stores `switchToggles`, `allowSwitchOff`, `defaultOnIndex`, or its own toggle normalization logic.
- Static compile check passed after the code change via `dotnet build BrainPunk/Assembly-CSharp.csproj --no-restore`: 0 errors.

### Pending validation

- Unity PlayMode still needs to verify that each `Config.Skin.SpineResource` value exactly matches a skin name in the `SkinViewer` Spine skeleton; this is currently inferred from config field purpose, not proven by runtime playback.
- Unity PlayMode still needs to verify `skin_free_btn`, `skin_coin_btn`, and `skin_purchase_btn` child button/text discovery on the production `ShopPanel.prefab`, including inactive object lookup.
- Unity PlayMode still needs to verify owned click apply, default skin ownership migration, ad unlock callback, coin insufficient/sufficient flows, purchase success/failure callbacks, close/reopen cleanup, and repeated selection while an ad or purchase is in progress.
- Android/iOS landscape smoke still needs to verify touch targets, action button placement, purchase SDK behavior, ad SDK callback behavior, and combined-skin viewer rendering on device.

## 2026-06-15: ShopPanel Skin version3.0.0 boxer switch flow

### Confirmed local evidence

- `tbskin.json` currently stores part skin `PrefabResource` values as `prefab1_*` for back, `prefab2_*` for face, and `prefab3_*` for body; the current part rows have empty `SpineResource`.
- Current `ShopPanel.prefab` skin preview uses an `actor` root containing `Boxer_Rt`, a preview `Camera`, and a nested `Actor` prefab instance. `Boxer_Rt` is a `RawImage` bound to `Assets/Game/UI/ShopPanel/boxer.renderTexture`; the preview `Camera.targetTexture` points to the same RenderTexture.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` now treats `GameObjectToggleGroup` as the owner of filter exclusivity and only maps selected index to all/back/face/body filtering.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` now saves part selections with `PrefabResource` when available, while full-body skins still save the Spine skin name fallback path.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` resolves saved part values by matching `Id`, `PrefabResource`, or `SpineResource`, so older saves that stored skin ids can still map back to the current config row.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart.ApplyCurrentSkinToViewer()` still contains the earlier `back`, `face`, and `shirt` `RectTransform` part apply path, but current `ShopPanel.prefab` leaves those fields unassigned and no longer provides confirmed `Hat`, `Face`, or `Shirt` UI part roots. Treat this part-attachment path as pending replacement by the RenderTexture actor path.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` treats the production `GameObjectToggleGroup` as the only owner of filter switch exclusivity; skin item re-click clearing is handled in the item apply path, not by allowing the filter toggle group to switch off.
- Clicking the currently applied owned skin clear path targets only that skin's saved field: `CurrentBackPart`, `CurrentFacePart`, `CurrentBodyPart`, or `CurrentSkinId`. Part clears destroy the matching boxer prefab instance; full-body clears restore `fallbackBaseSkinName` when configured.
- Boxer part resource loading no longer derives asset paths from `prefab1_*`, `prefab2_*`, or `prefab3_*`. Runtime loading uses the matched `Config.Skin.PrefabResource` value directly as the YooAsset prefab location.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` checks prefab locations through `Bear.ResourceSystem.ResourceManager.CanLoad<GameObject>()` before calling `ResourceManager.LoadAsync<GameObject>(location)`, avoiding the loader failure branch for invalid locations.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` caches loaded boxer prefabs by `PrefabResource`, instantiates one child under the target boxer part container, resets transform to local zero/identity/one, stretches UI `RectTransform` prefab instances to their container, and destroys previous/current instances on part clear, close, or destroy.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` now exposes explicit boxer preview references for `Camera`, `RawImage`, `RenderTexture`, actor root, and `ActorSpineCtrl`. Runtime reference resolution falls back to the current prefab object names `Camera`, `Boxer_Rt`, and `Actor`, plus the first child `ActorSpineCtrl`, so the preview lifecycle can work before all fields are manually assigned in the prefab.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` enables the boxer preview camera and clears the RenderTexture on enable, then clears the RenderTexture and disables the preview camera on disable/destroy to avoid stale frames and background rendering while SkinPart is inactive.
- `Main.unity` contains a root `Skin` object that is inactive by default and owns the scene-side boxer preview, including `SkinRt_Camera` with `boxer.renderTexture` assigned. `ShopPanel_SkinPart` now resolves this root from loaded scene root objects by name, activates it while SkinPart is active, and deactivates it on SkinPart disable/destroy.
- `ShopPanel.OnClose()` now calls `ShopPanel_SkinPart.HideSceneSkinPreview()` as a close-path guard so the scene `Skin` object is set inactive when the ShopPanel is destroyed, even if the Skin tab is not currently active.
- `Main.unity` scene `Skin` root now serializes `m_IsActive: 0`, so the preview starts inactive before the ShopPanel Skin flow activates it.
- The scene actor mount points currently used by boxer part previews are lowercase `back`, `face`, and `body` GameObjects under the Actor prefab instance; they are normal `Transform` objects with BoneFollower/BoneFollowerAutoBinder components, not `RectTransform` UI nodes.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` resolves lowercase `back`, `face`, and `body` first, then keeps uppercase/legacy fallback names. The mount lookup now returns `Transform`, so these scene BoneFollower nodes can be found.
- `ShopPanel_SkinPart` keeps scene `Skin` camera/actor references scoped to the scene root, but it preserves the ShopPanel-local `Boxer_Rt` RawImage reference because that RawImage is the UI display target for the same `boxer.renderTexture`.
- Static compile check passed after the v3 change via `dotnet build BrainPunk/Assembly-CSharp.csproj --no-restore`: 0 errors.
- Static compile check passed again after the scene mount/RawImage fix: 0 errors / 90 existing warnings.

### Pending validation

- Generated runtime `Assets/Game/Configs/tbskin.json` and source `Luban/Configs/Datas/#Skin.xlsx` still show many legacy `prefab1_*`, `prefab2_*`, and `prefab3_*` values. Existing prefab files under `Assets/Game/Prefabs/Skins` currently match only `Sp_zs_bak_img_001`, `Sp_zs_fz_img_001`, and `Sp_zs_mb_img_002`; remaining rows need config/resource completion before all skin previews can load.
- Unity PlayMode still needs to verify that the production YooAsset `GamePackage` can load each `Config.Skin.PrefabResource` prefab location directly.
- Unity PlayMode still needs to verify default/empty saved part values hide only the boxer part container and do not break the bone follower parent.
- Unity PlayMode still needs to verify unlock/apply for back, face, body, and full-body rows; close/reopen should restore the saved boxer composition.
- Unity PlayMode still needs to verify that disabling the SkinPart camera does not interfere with the panel's show/hide timing, and that clearing `boxer.renderTexture` does not produce a visible flash when the Skin tab opens.
- Unity PlayMode still needs to verify that `ShopPanel_SkinPart` binds the scene `Skin` object's `SkinRt_Camera`, actor root, and part roots instead of stale serialized references from the ShopPanel prefab.
- Android/iOS landscape smoke still needs to verify boxer part prefab layering, scale, and no visible hitch on first prefab load.

