- `Assets/Game/Prefabs/LevelItems/Actor/Actor.prefab` now has `ActorSkinBinding` wired to its existing `ActorCtrl`, `ActorSpineCtrl`, and lowercase `back`, `face`, and inner `body` BoneFollower mount transforms.
- `Actor.prefab` contains both an outer Spine visual root named `body` and an inner part mount named `body`; the binder's automatic fallback mount lookup prefers same-name transforms that have `BoneFollowerAutoBinder` or `BoneFollower`.
- `Actor_infiniteJump.prefab` was inspected and not wired in this pass because it currently lacks the back/face/body BoneFollower part mount structure required for gameplay part prefab binding.
- Static compile after the Actor skin binding implementation passed via `dotnet build BrainPunk/Assembly-CSharp.csproj --no-restore`: 0 errors / 90 existing warnings.

